<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/todo-takatora"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/todo-takatora.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tōdō Takatora</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Tōdō Takatora (1556–1630) was a Japanese warlord who served several masters, including Toyotomi Hideyoshi, before siding with Tokugawa Ieyasu at Sekigahara in 1600.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/todor-zhivkov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/todor-zhivkov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Todor Zhivkov</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Todor Zhivkov was the communist leader of Bulgaria for 35 years, first secretary of the Bulgarian Communist Party from 1954 to 1989 and head of state from 1971.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/toera"><span class="enc-name">Toera</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Toera was the last king of the Sakalava kingdom of Menabe in western Madagascar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tofangchi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tofangchi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tofangchi</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Tofangchi were musketeers in the armies of Safavid and later Iranian states.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/toffa-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/toffa-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Toffa I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Toffa I was king of Porto-Novo, on the coast of present-day Benin, from 1874 until his death in 1908.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedi